  "title": "The dir() Function",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Course: Learn Python Intermediate"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "The dir() Function"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The dir() function lists out all the attributes and methods of the given object. For example,"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "content": "1number = 1\n2print(dir(number))"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Output"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "['__abs__', '__add__', '__and__', '__bool__', '__ceil__', '__class__', '__delattr__', '__dir__', '__divmod__', '__doc__', '__eq__', '__float__', '__floor__', '__floordiv__', '__format__', '__ge__', '__getattribute__', '__getnewargs__', '__gt__', ......]"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "This means, any integer like 1 (which is an object of the int class) can access all these methods and attributes."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Let's try to use this __add__() method in our code."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "content": "1number = 5\n2\n3result = number.__add__(100)\n4print(result)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Output"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "105"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "As we can see, the __add__() method can be used for addition."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "In fact, the + operator internally calls this __add__() method for addition. The above code is equivalent to:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "content": "1number = 5\n2\n3result = number + 100\n4print(result)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "At the surface, it may look like the + operator is working like how it works in mathematics, but internally it's calling the __add__() method for addition."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "How does it work?"
    },
